01:00:23.360 --> 01:00:25.480
were the subject of a documentary film

01:00:25.480 --> 01:00:28.520
called Silenced by Jim Spione.

01:00:28.520 --> 01:00:29.600
That ended up doing well.

01:00:29.600 --> 01:00:32.160
It had quite a long run on Netflix and Amazon

01:00:32.160 --> 01:00:34.760
and was nominated for an Emmy Award.

01:00:34.760 --> 01:00:38.840
That's another thing that I'll be forever grateful for

01:00:38.840 --> 01:00:41.640
was Jim Spione coming into my home that year

01:00:41.640 --> 01:00:44.160
and really telling the story.

01:00:45.720 --> 01:00:47.200
It was also brave on his part

01:00:47.200 --> 01:00:48.520
because there were so many people

01:00:48.520 --> 01:00:50.960
who didn't want to touch either one of our stories.

01:00:50.960 --> 01:00:51.800
Yes, absolutely.

01:00:51.800 --> 01:00:55.120
Many were afraid to, they were afraid of the truth.

01:00:55.120 --> 01:00:56.600
Has that changed by now?

01:00:57.600 --> 01:01:01.840
I think there is a growing awareness in terms,

01:01:01.840 --> 01:01:03.960
I mean, that's one of the sort of the silver linings

01:01:03.960 --> 01:01:05.160
in all of this.

01:01:05.160 --> 01:01:09.400
The publicity itself, the fact that it's become

01:01:09.400 --> 01:01:14.200
more publicly known helps people inform themselves

01:01:14.200 --> 01:01:16.200
in terms of what's at stake.

01:01:16.200 --> 01:01:18.680
The question is, what will people do with the information?

01:01:18.680 --> 01:01:21.080
And power does not yield itself, right?

01:01:21.080 --> 01:01:24.400
Willing, it's not gonna give up power very easily.

01:01:24.440 --> 01:01:26.600
If anything, it's gonna protect it and grow it.

01:01:26.600 --> 01:01:29.400
And so no matter where that power comes from.

01:01:29.400 --> 01:01:32.520
But yes, the documentary silence was in fact,

01:01:32.520 --> 01:01:35.280
it highlighted John's case, my case,

01:01:35.280 --> 01:01:37.200
as well as Jess and Radax.

01:01:37.200 --> 01:01:41.320
There was another PBS, the US PBS frontline,

01:01:41.320 --> 01:01:43.680
did United States of Secrets.

01:01:43.680 --> 01:01:45.040
It was a three hour special

01:01:45.040 --> 01:01:48.640
in which I was threaded throughout the first two hours.

01:01:48.640 --> 01:01:52.040
And it also had extensive interviews

01:01:52.080 --> 01:01:55.880
with Bill Binney and Kirk Wiebe and Diane Bork and Ed Loomis,

01:01:55.880 --> 01:01:57.600
the other NSA whistleblowers.

01:01:57.600 --> 01:02:01.480
I was ultimately the only one charged on the Esmeajak.

01:02:01.480 --> 01:02:03.200
And it would be remiss for me.

01:02:03.200 --> 01:02:05.960
I mean, there's some, it is surreal for me to say this,

01:02:05.960 --> 01:02:10.800
but even Jelson Radak, when I was so publicly charged,

01:02:10.800 --> 01:02:14.080
and then publicly indicted after being secretly charged

01:02:14.080 --> 01:02:16.840
by the government for having quote, unquote,

01:02:16.840 --> 01:02:20.080
exposed state secrets, that was all,

01:02:20.640 --> 01:02:23.080
had five counts of the Esmeajak against me

01:02:23.080 --> 01:02:26.520
and obstruction of justice and making false statements

01:02:26.520 --> 01:02:28.680
which in themselves were false.

01:02:28.680 --> 01:02:33.720
That whole thing was framed, of course, by the FBI,

01:02:33.720 --> 01:02:36.280
which also raises other questions

01:02:36.280 --> 01:02:39.960
about those who ostensibly stand up for the truth.

01:02:41.440 --> 01:02:44.680
But when I was so publicly indicted, the only person,

01:02:44.680 --> 01:02:46.480
she knew there was one person at a time,

01:02:46.480 --> 01:02:48.600
you have to remember, it's kind of hard for me

01:02:48.600 --> 01:02:50.680
even it's all these years have gone by now,

01:02:50.680 --> 01:02:53.000
that was the spring of 2010.

01:02:53.000 --> 01:02:56.080
So I was only the fourth American at that time

01:02:57.280 --> 01:03:00.480
who had been charged as a non spy,

01:03:00.480 --> 01:03:04.120
but under the Esmeajak, the first person was Ellsberg.

01:03:05.040 --> 01:03:08.360
And she knew there was only a universe of one

01:03:08.360 --> 01:03:10.320
who understood exactly what I was going through.

01:03:10.320 --> 01:03:12.400
And so she introduced me to Ellsberg,

01:03:12.400 --> 01:03:16.840
I actually met him at DC not long after I was indicted

01:03:16.880 --> 01:03:18.440
and we hit it off right away.

01:03:20.280 --> 01:03:23.360
And then of course, full circle silver lining,

01:03:23.360 --> 01:03:27.200
I did plead out 240 hours community service,

01:03:27.200 --> 01:03:30.240
one year probation, and although the judge didn't know

01:03:30.240 --> 01:03:32.520
at the time, I ended up interviewing veterans

01:03:32.520 --> 01:03:34.840
from World War II to the present day

01:03:34.840 --> 01:03:36.720
and probably one of the most extraordinary

01:03:36.720 --> 01:03:38.600
of the interviews, it was the longest one

01:03:38.600 --> 01:03:41.680
for the Veterans History Project, the Library of Congress.

01:03:41.680 --> 01:03:43.360
No one had interviewed them

01:03:43.360 --> 01:03:45.640
for the Library of Congress's Veterans History Project

01:03:45.680 --> 01:03:46.600
until I came along.

01:03:46.600 --> 01:03:49.080
And so I had about a six hour plus interview

01:03:49.080 --> 01:03:51.080
with Ellsberg in his home, you know,

01:03:51.080 --> 01:03:52.560
out in Northern California.

01:03:52.560 --> 01:03:53.680
It was an extraordinary interview.

01:03:53.680 --> 01:03:56.160
If you go out to the Library of Congress website,

01:03:57.120 --> 01:03:59.240
Veterans History Project,

01:03:59.240 --> 01:04:01.080
you'll actually see the interview

01:04:01.080 --> 01:04:04.080
as well as about three and a half dozen other veterans.

01:04:04.080 --> 01:04:05.040
Okay.

01:04:05.040 --> 01:04:10.040
Now, Ellsberg is now regarded as one of the most,

01:04:11.040 --> 01:04:14.520
as a journalist of the most integrity,

01:04:14.520 --> 01:04:16.280
pretty much out there.

01:04:16.280 --> 01:04:20.520
And I feel the same way about you,

01:04:21.840 --> 01:04:26.280
both of you, the way you're keeping awareness going

01:04:26.280 --> 01:04:28.800
and relaying your own story.

01:04:28.800 --> 01:04:32.000
Now, before you joined, Thomas,

01:04:32.000 --> 01:04:34.040
John and I were talking about what's happening

01:04:34.040 --> 01:04:36.080
currently with the OPCW

01:04:36.920 --> 01:04:41.920
and presumed a poison gas attack in Douma, Syria,

01:04:43.000 --> 01:04:45.600
which wasn't a poison gas attack,

01:04:45.600 --> 01:04:49.320
was a fake report, pretty much.

01:04:49.320 --> 01:04:51.560
Nobody's reporting on that.

01:04:51.560 --> 01:04:55.080
So press still is not reporting on new stories

01:04:55.080 --> 01:04:55.920
the way I see it.

01:04:55.920 --> 01:04:57.080
How do you look at that?

01:04:58.800 --> 01:05:00.800
Well, unfortunately we have too much of the press.

01:05:00.800 --> 01:05:03.080
It doesn't really want to get to the truth

01:05:03.080 --> 01:05:05.080
of what's behind the news.

01:05:05.080 --> 01:05:08.120
In fact, this is very Orwellian where you have Newspeak

01:05:08.120 --> 01:05:10.520
where you present...

01:05:10.520 --> 01:05:11.360
Hang on.

01:05:12.200 --> 01:05:14.480
Hang on, do you want to say something?

01:05:14.480 --> 01:05:15.920
Oh, sure.

01:05:15.920 --> 01:05:18.000
I'm sorry, I didn't mean to interrupt.

01:05:18.000 --> 01:05:19.800
I just, I have to leave for work.

01:05:19.800 --> 01:05:21.920
So for me, I've got to go.

01:05:21.920 --> 01:05:24.640
Great to see all of you.

01:05:24.640 --> 01:05:26.400
Have a happy new year.

01:05:26.400 --> 01:05:27.760
All the best of luck in January.

01:05:27.760 --> 01:05:28.880
We'll talk again.

01:05:28.880 --> 01:05:29.720
I look forward to it.

01:05:29.720 --> 01:05:30.560
Bye-bye, guys.

01:05:30.560 --> 01:05:31.400
Take care, John.

01:05:31.400 --> 01:05:32.240
Take care.

01:05:32.240 --> 01:05:33.080
Bye-bye, Tom.

01:05:33.080 --> 01:05:34.400
Yeah.

01:05:34.400 --> 01:05:39.400
He was too modest, too much a gentleman to interrupt.

01:05:39.400 --> 01:05:42.520
But we had to say goodbye to him.

01:05:42.520 --> 01:05:44.720
Okay, carry on, Thomas.

01:05:44.720 --> 01:05:47.880
Well, Eric Blair, aka George Orwell, right, his pen name.

01:05:49.360 --> 01:05:51.120
You know, he was a freedom fighter.

01:05:51.120 --> 01:05:53.280
He was a repentant colonial officer.

01:05:53.280 --> 01:05:55.520
He had seen what happens with empire.

01:05:56.400 --> 01:05:58.680
He had seen what happens when freedoms

01:05:58.680 --> 01:06:00.540
are taken away from other people.

01:06:00.540 --> 01:06:02.080
And he began to write about it.

01:06:02.080 --> 01:06:05.320
And, you know, the famous 1984 book,

01:06:05.320 --> 01:06:08.400
which to me is more relevant now than ever.

01:06:08.400 --> 01:06:10.960
It's something I've actually lived on a very personal level.

01:06:10.960 --> 01:06:13.000
I keep, that's one thing I keep putting out there

01:06:13.000 --> 01:06:16.160
when I talk to people as I go around the world

01:06:16.160 --> 01:06:19.960
to various conferences and in front of university students

01:06:19.960 --> 01:06:23.000
and other fora.

01:06:23.000 --> 01:06:25.480
I bring up 1984.

01:06:25.480 --> 01:06:27.880
And it's not just science fiction.

01:06:27.880 --> 01:06:29.880
He saw, I think he really did see

01:06:29.880 --> 01:06:31.120
based on his own experiences.

01:06:31.120 --> 01:06:33.640
I mean, context is everything.

01:06:33.640 --> 01:06:37.120
But in many cases, things have actually gotten far worse

01:06:37.120 --> 01:06:38.680
even since he wrote that book.

01:06:38.680 --> 01:06:43.000
And although 1984 is actually a few decades ago,

01:06:43.000 --> 01:06:44.760
it's actually more relevant now than ever.

01:06:44.760 --> 01:06:48.300
And he referred to something called news speak.

01:06:48.300 --> 01:06:50.360
And it's sort of a double entendre, right?

01:06:50.360 --> 01:06:53.640
That news is not necessarily real news.

01:06:53.640 --> 01:06:56.000
The news is intended to manipulate.

01:06:56.000 --> 01:06:59.400
And so often what passes as news is really propaganda.

01:06:59.400 --> 01:07:02.520
And propaganda, especially when you wrap the truth

01:07:02.520 --> 01:07:05.240
in a body of lies to quote, unquote, protect it.

01:07:05.240 --> 01:07:09.000
I put air quotes around protect, really to hide it,

01:07:09.000 --> 01:07:10.920
becomes extraordinarily dangerous

01:07:10.920 --> 01:07:13.560
because then you get people to believe it.

01:07:13.560 --> 01:07:15.480
And when you get people to believe propaganda

01:07:15.480 --> 01:07:16.640
as if it were the truth,

01:07:16.640 --> 01:07:19.320
then that's a form of the big lie.

01:07:20.240 --> 01:07:22.960
And history's not kind when it comes to big lies,

01:07:22.960 --> 01:07:24.920
but it's meant to manipulate.

01:07:24.920 --> 01:07:28.200
It's meant to manage perceptions.

01:07:28.800 --> 01:07:30.320
It's meant to divide people.

01:07:30.320 --> 01:07:34.880
It's meant to cause confusion,

01:07:34.880 --> 01:07:36.680
something from my military,

01:07:36.680 --> 01:07:39.240
but, you know, fog, uncertainty and doubt.

01:07:40.200 --> 01:07:41.720
And then it's like, well, what's the truth?

01:07:41.720 --> 01:07:43.080
How do I know what is true?

01:07:43.080 --> 01:07:47.440
And it really takes dogged investigative journalism

01:07:47.440 --> 01:07:48.760
to get behind the truth.

01:07:48.760 --> 01:07:50.760
And that's not always easy,

01:07:50.760 --> 01:07:52.500
especially when it comes to power.

01:07:53.520 --> 01:07:55.940
Power wants to protect itself.

01:07:55.940 --> 01:07:59.540
And my concern is that increasingly

01:07:59.540 --> 01:08:04.540
you have organs of government and organs of the press

01:08:04.580 --> 01:08:08.860
who simply begin to spout the lies of those in power.

01:08:08.860 --> 01:08:10.540
And it's very concerning,

01:08:10.540 --> 01:08:15.540
especially when you have mainstream platforming, right?

01:08:16.100 --> 01:08:17.940
But you also have a number of others,

01:08:17.940 --> 01:08:19.420
so-called independence,

01:08:19.420 --> 01:08:22.500
who themselves fall into the same trap.

01:08:22.500 --> 01:08:25.260
It's like both sides end up engaging

01:08:25.260 --> 01:08:27.940
in a very similar way,

01:08:27.940 --> 01:08:29.940
sort of the narrative counter-narrative.

01:08:30.940 --> 01:08:33.500
And the narrative is not,

01:08:33.500 --> 01:08:35.700
it doesn't matter what the facts are.

01:08:35.700 --> 01:08:38.700
And in fact, what are its representative facts

01:08:38.700 --> 01:08:41.500
are usually intended to maintain the official narrative.

01:08:41.500 --> 01:08:43.300
So the narrative becomes a story

01:08:43.300 --> 01:08:47.540
that turns into what's supposed to be the truth.

01:08:47.540 --> 01:08:51.460
And then the truth is actually propagated as a lie,

01:08:51.460 --> 01:08:54.340
but you're supposed to believe it as the truth.

01:08:54.340 --> 01:08:55.560
So it doesn't really matter?

01:08:55.560 --> 01:08:58.620
Well, no, facts don't have anything to do

01:08:58.620 --> 01:09:01.740
with actually exposing the truth.

01:09:01.740 --> 01:09:04.100
Then we're all living a fiction.

01:09:04.100 --> 01:09:05.580
And I think that's the real concern

01:09:05.580 --> 01:09:07.540
and that's what Orwell addressed, right?

01:09:07.540 --> 01:09:10.220
What kind of reality are we living in?

01:09:10.220 --> 01:09:13.540
Well, let's turn that to a real-life example

01:09:13.540 --> 01:09:17.180
of something I cannot understand what's going on.

01:09:17.180 --> 01:09:19.660
What's with that Trump whistleblower situation?

01:09:20.980 --> 01:09:23.660
Well, this is where I do believe

01:09:23.660 --> 01:09:26.940
and there's some interesting dynamics.

01:09:28.180 --> 01:09:33.180
Member, I accept that there is a person

01:09:33.180 --> 01:09:35.340
and there are names out, there's a name out there,

01:09:35.340 --> 01:09:38.980
there's actually more than one whistleblower, quote unquote.

01:09:38.980 --> 01:09:42.100
I do accept, what's interesting about this

01:09:42.100 --> 01:09:46.340
is if you're looking at how Trump has reacted in others,

01:09:47.220 --> 01:09:49.180
then there's gotta be something

01:09:49.180 --> 01:09:52.700
that was actually said-shared through channels

01:09:52.700 --> 01:09:55.140
that must be at least close to the truth.

01:09:55.140 --> 01:09:59.220
Why would there be such an extraordinary response

01:09:59.220 --> 01:10:00.220
to take out-

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:04.360
and take down the whistleblower, whistleblowers.

01:10:04.360 --> 01:10:07.120
Look, I went through the same type of channels.

01:10:07.120 --> 01:10:09.840
I actually went, it was the Intelligence Community

01:10:09.840 --> 01:10:12.360
Whistleblower Protection Act has been updated

01:10:12.360 --> 01:10:17.200
since my whistleblowing, except this one actually

01:10:17.200 --> 01:10:17.960
made the press.

01:10:17.960 --> 01:10:19.880
In my case, it was suppressed.

01:10:19.880 --> 01:10:22.840
I went to Congress, but everything was suppressed.

01:10:22.840 --> 01:10:24.840
And it's surreal for me, because I

01:10:24.840 --> 01:10:28.880
was speaking about crimes that were actually willfully

01:10:28.880 --> 01:10:30.320
committed by the up to and including

01:10:30.320 --> 01:10:33.280
the president of the United States and those around them.

01:10:33.280 --> 01:10:34.840
Highest levels of government.

01:10:34.840 --> 01:10:36.800
They were actually impeachable offenses.

01:10:36.800 --> 01:10:38.680
They were in violation of the Constitution,

01:10:38.680 --> 01:10:42.320
but it didn't rise to a level what Congress cared,

01:10:42.320 --> 01:10:44.320
because they were in on it.

01:10:44.320 --> 01:10:47.560
They were in on letting the executive branch

01:10:47.560 --> 01:10:49.760
have extraordinary sway.

01:10:49.760 --> 01:10:52.080
Here, it's become highly politicized.

01:10:52.080 --> 01:10:53.960
There, you had both sides.

01:10:53.960 --> 01:10:56.720
So now, you're weaponizing each side against the other.

01:10:56.720 --> 01:10:58.520
And it's just quite extraordinary.

01:10:58.800 --> 01:11:00.480
We've actually, the president is impeached.

01:11:00.480 --> 01:11:04.640
That will always be on the historical record.

01:11:04.640 --> 01:11:07.600
Whether or not he's acquitted or found guilty,

01:11:07.600 --> 01:11:10.240
we don't know yet.

01:11:10.240 --> 01:11:11.960
The articles have not been turned over.

01:11:11.960 --> 01:11:16.080
It's a very interesting clause within the Constitution

01:11:16.080 --> 01:11:19.520
in terms of our system of governance.

01:11:19.520 --> 01:11:20.840
But it's just extraordinary.

01:11:20.840 --> 01:11:26.320
The weaponization of truth and lies, it's both.

01:11:26.320 --> 01:11:27.760
So how do you tell the difference?

01:11:27.800 --> 01:11:31.600
This is where, and I'm the first to acknowledge

01:11:31.600 --> 01:11:33.680
that if you look at those in Congress

01:11:33.680 --> 01:11:35.040
that are in positions of power,

01:11:35.040 --> 01:11:36.920
there's a lot of hypocrisy.

01:11:36.920 --> 01:11:39.080
Because where were they when I blew the whistle?

01:11:39.080 --> 01:11:40.400
Where were they?

01:11:40.400 --> 01:11:43.400
Look, some of the people running for president right now,

01:11:43.400 --> 01:11:47.400
including Bernie Sanders, literally crickets

01:11:47.400 --> 01:11:50.920
when directly approached about my case,

01:11:50.920 --> 01:11:52.160
would not touch it.

01:11:53.240 --> 01:11:54.680
Wonder why, right?

01:11:54.680 --> 01:11:56.240
This is Bernie Sanders, right?

01:11:57.080 --> 01:11:59.320
I used to live in Vermont.

01:11:59.320 --> 01:12:03.080
I remember growing up when he was the mayor of Burlington.

01:12:04.200 --> 01:12:07.480
But he would not say anything.

01:12:07.480 --> 01:12:08.440
He would not.

01:12:10.360 --> 01:12:13.960
My perspective here on the politicians is quite cynical.

01:12:13.960 --> 01:12:18.960
Even those who apparently adhere to a message

01:12:21.720 --> 01:12:24.200
that resonates with, in this case with Bernie

01:12:24.240 --> 01:12:26.800
with a working class, quote unquote,

01:12:26.800 --> 01:12:30.960
I just have to take everything any politician says

01:12:30.960 --> 01:12:34.400
with significant grains of salt.

01:12:34.400 --> 01:12:35.240
All right.

01:12:35.240 --> 01:12:37.520
Just before we continue,

01:12:37.520 --> 01:12:39.320
allow me to introduce somebody you know already.

01:12:39.320 --> 01:12:40.640
Here's Bailey.

01:12:40.640 --> 01:12:41.480
Ah, Bailey.

01:12:41.480 --> 01:12:43.600
You have to take it out of, yeah, there you go.

01:12:43.600 --> 01:12:44.800
Hey, Bailey.

01:12:44.800 --> 01:12:46.000
Hello.

01:12:46.000 --> 01:12:47.440
Hey, Bailey.

01:12:47.440 --> 01:12:48.880
Hey, mom.

01:12:48.880 --> 01:12:49.800
So for the audience,

01:12:49.800 --> 01:12:52.320
this is Bailey LeMond calling in from Canada.

01:12:53.280 --> 01:12:54.120
All right.

01:12:54.120 --> 01:12:54.960
And you...

01:12:54.960 --> 01:12:56.920
Yeah, our friendly, our friendly Northern neighbor

01:12:56.920 --> 01:12:58.400
that we, you know, we have the longest,

01:12:58.400 --> 01:13:00.120
well, now it's semi-guarded,

01:13:00.120 --> 01:13:03.760
but the longest border between two countries

01:13:03.760 --> 01:13:05.160
that doesn't have,

01:13:05.160 --> 01:13:07.600
well, there aren't some fences along the border,

01:13:07.600 --> 01:13:10.160
but yet I consider, I consider,

01:13:10.160 --> 01:13:11.160
I really like Canada.

01:13:11.160 --> 01:13:12.400
I've been to Canada a few times.

01:13:12.400 --> 01:13:14.440
So yeah, welcome, Bailey.

01:13:14.440 --> 01:13:15.400
Thank you.

01:13:15.400 --> 01:13:16.960
We were just coming out of a conversation

01:13:16.960 --> 01:13:18.800
about the Trump whistleblower

01:13:18.800 --> 01:13:21.160
and Thomas touched upon impeachment.

01:13:21.160 --> 01:13:23.480
Thomas, I wanted to ask you,

01:13:23.480 --> 01:13:26.080
even impeachment appears to be weaponized now.

01:13:26.080 --> 01:13:30.240
Yes, I, yes, it does.

